<div class="ah-container ah-container--centered">
  <div class="ah-card ah-jev-card">
    <div class="ah-logo">&#x1F9E9;</div>
    <h1 class="ah-title">Case 09 &mdash; Jev (TypeSafe AI)</h1>
    <p class="ah-subtitle">
      Not a chat model &mdash; Jev evaluates whatever you type against 4 fixed
      questions in one call and returns typed, probabilistic answers.
    </p>

    <div class="ah-jev-layout">
      <div class="ah-jev-main">
        <%= render "form" %>

        <div class="ah-jev-section-label">Final result</div>
        <div id="ah-jev-summary" class="ah-result ah-jev-summary">
          <span class="ah-placeholder">Summary will appear here&hellip;</span>
        </div>

        <div class="ah-jev-section-label">Full response structure</div>
        <%= render "result" %>
      </div>

      <div class="ah-jev-aside">
        <p class="ah-jev-hint">
          <strong>What to type:</strong> any piece of text you'd want a system to
          triage automatically &mdash; a support ticket, a product review, a forum
          comment, a chat message. Try something clearly positive, something
          angry/urgent, and something with hostile language to see all four
          scores move.
        </p>

        <div class="ah-jev-section-label">Questions asked</div>
        <ul class="ah-jev-questions">
          <li><strong>sentiment</strong> (score, 5 levels) &mdash; how positive the tone is</li>
          <li><strong>topic</strong> (choice) &mdash; support / feedback / spam</li>
          <li><strong>urgent</strong> (noul) &mdash; does this need a fast response</li>
          <li><strong>harmful</strong> (noul) &mdash; hate speech, threats, harassment, or other dangerous content</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="ah-jev-section-label">Question format sent to Jev</div>
        <pre class="ah-jev-code"><code><%= JSON.pretty_generate(JevRequest::QUESTIONS) %></code></pre>

        <p class="ah-jev-hint">
          <strong>Moderation, specifically:</strong> yes &mdash; a plain
          <code>noul</code> question with instructions like "does this contain
          hate speech, threats, or dangerous content?" is exactly how you'd use
          Jev for comment/content moderation. The <code>harmful</code> row
          demonstrates it directly; swap the wording in
          <code>JevRequest::QUESTIONS</code> to target whatever policy you're
          enforcing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <%= render "nav",
         back_label: "&larr; Case 08",
         back_path:  ai_requests_transcribe_path,
         next_label: "Cases &rarr;",
         next_path:  ai_cases_path %>
  </div>
</div>

<% content_for :styles do %>
  <style>
    .ah-jev-section-label {
      width: 100%;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #8b98ac;
      margin: 0.9rem 0 0.4rem;
    }
    .ah-jev-summary {
      min-height: 0;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .ah-jev-row {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      padding: 0.3rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(200, 210, 230, 0.5);
    }
    .ah-jev-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .ah-jev-row-label {
      font-weight: 600;
      color: #4a5a70;
      text-transform: capitalize;
    }
    .ah-jev-row-value {
      color: #2c3e50;
      text-align: right;
    }
    .ah-jev-hint {
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      background: rgba(240, 244, 255, 0.6);
      border: 1px solid rgba(200, 210, 230, 0.6);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
    }
    .ah-jev-questions {
      width: 100%;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: #4a5a70;
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
    }
    .ah-jev-questions li { margin: 0.2rem 0; }
    .ah-jev-code {
      width: 100%;
      max-height: 260px;
      overflow: auto;
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
      background: rgba(44, 62, 80, 0.92);
      color: #d9e6f5;
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 0.8rem 0.9rem;
      margin: 0;
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    /* This page has a lot more content than the other cases (a two-column
       layout with explainer text + 2 result sections). The shared layout
       fixes html/body/.ah-container to exactly 100vh with overflow:hidden
       and .ah-card to a narrow fixed width, which is fine for short forms
       but clips this page and disables scrolling. Override for this page
       only — don't touch the shared CSS, every other case still relies on
       the fixed-viewport behavior. */
    html, body {
      height: auto;
      min-height: 100%;
      overflow-y: auto;
    }
    .ah-container {
      height: auto;
      min-height: 100vh;
      padding: 2.5rem 0;
    }
    .ah-jev-card {
      width: min(1280px, 97vw);
    }

    .ah-jev-layout {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 2rem;
      width: 100%;
    }
    .ah-jev-main {
      flex: 1 1 55%;
      min-width: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    .ah-jev-aside {
      flex: 1 1 45%;
      min-width: 0;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
      gap: 0.4rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      .ah-jev-layout { flex-direction: column; }
    }
  </style>
<% end %>

<% content_for :scripts do %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "ai_request_jev" %>
<% end %>
